hello and congratulations on your  exhibition  at the upcoming virtual event  on behalf of lab roots we are very  excited to be working with you and  putting together your virtual booth  for the upcoming virtual event at this  point  you should have received your booth  materials which contain the booth grid  that we will be covering  this video will take you through your  booth grid  the booth grid contains sections you  will fill out with your company's  information  and then send to us along with any  virtual booth assets  such as logos images pdf documents  videos and anything else we might need  to build out your virtual booth  not all fields or sections are mandatory  but all of it is recommended to make  your booth  look and feel more interactive let's get  started  the first page of the booth grid is a  general overview  there is a field here to enter your  booth's objectives to help us understand  what you want to achieve with your booth  in this virtual event and allow us to  make any recommendations that may be  helpful to you  in achieving your booth objectives and  goals  below the objectives field is a table of  contents for your reference  and below that is the hightail upload  link where you'll be able to upload your  booth grid once you have completed it  as well as any files we'll need for the  booth building process  pages 2 and 3 contain the virtual booth  reference overview of design elements  information and features please use this  as a reference guide to help you  identify the sections that you are  working on in the booth grid  the first section of the booth grid is  the company contact information  please keep in mind that this is the  information an attendee who visits your  booth will find  if they have any questions or inquiries  and not what the booth builder would use  to contact you  with any questions or concerns during  your booth building process  section 2 is the about us field where  you have up to 2 000 characters maximum  including spaces to describe your  company  we can also hyperlink urls to send  attendees out to an external site  where they can view more information  about your company section 3 is the  booth template and booth floor  you'll first need to take a look at the  booth template images to choose from  on pages 9-12 and floor options on page  14.  once you've selected your booth and  floor you can fill in the booth template  number and floor number  so your booth production builder knows  which templates to use to build out your  booth  section 4 is the booth background in  windows you'll find the background  options on page 15  and window options on page 14. please  fill in your selections in section 4.  section 5 is the booth chat features you  can select one or all of these  booth chat features depending on what  you are looking for the choices are  public chat  one-to-one chat private chat video chat  virtual badge chat queue and info card  the public chat is something we do  standardly across the board  for all booths but this is still an  option whether you want to include it or  not  public chat is where all attendees and  all booth reps can chat in one area  and will be seen by anyone and everyone  who visits your booth  this is a great way to start up  conversations and from here take an  attendee  into a private chat depending on what  they are looking for and questions they  may have  one-on-one chat and private chat  features allow  attendees and a live booth  representative to connect directly  but the private chat will not save any  transcripts  we now offer a video chat option for a  more personal conversation  a virtual badge is a great option if you  decide not to include any live virtual  booth representative  on the live event date when attendee  clicks on the virtual badge a  notification will be sent to an email of  your choice  where you will then be able to follow up  via email with an attendee  a chat queue is helpful if you do have a  live virtual booth representative on the  live event date  when the attendee clicks on the chat  queue they will be added to the queue of  waiting attendees in the virtual booth  representative dashboard  where a representative will be able to  see who is waiting to chat and from  there engage in a chat with an attendee  and lastly is the info card this is a  cool feature which allows attendees to  see more information  on the representative who they might be  chatting with this information can be  helpful to an attendee  if they have a specific question or  inquiry and can contact that  representative directly  on page five step six is social media  you can choose up to five social media  sites that your company might be signed  up on  to provide within your booth for  attendees to click on  this will take an attendee to an  external window outside of the event so  please keep that in mind  you can choose from facebook twitter  linkedin  instagram pinterest youtube or  enter any social media site not listed  here  section 7 is the booth representative  sign up  we will need the first and last name of  your booth representatives  as well as their email addresses to get  them set up on the backend  and give them access prior to the  virtual event date so that they can get  familiar with the booth representative  dashboard  section 8 is a booth representative  image you find all the reference booth  rep image options on page 16.  fill in the rep number you selected or  you can use  a custom rep image specifications are  listed if you would like to use an image  that is not provided in the booth grid  or would like to personalize it and  provide an image of a person who works  at your company  sections 9 10 11 are the small screen  and large screen options  you'll see that located within each  booth template are two small screens and  one large screen  you can place a static image within each  screen which can be clickable to a click  action  a content screen a rotating banner or a  doorway link  a click action allows a screen to be  clickable to an external url  or a single piece of content keep in  mind that  external urls can be opened up in an  iframe  or can send an attendee out to a new  window  a content screen would open a content  window  where attendees can view multiple pieces  of content  such as web links pdf documents videos  and webinars that can be listed  the rotating banner consists of multiple  images  that can also be clickable only to an  external url  but cannot link content lastly  is the doorway link a doorway link will  send attendees to a separate area in the  virtual environment  for any questions on click action  customizations  please inquire with your sales  representative  section 13 is the booth greeting this  option is a great way to greet attendees  which is  automatically shown to visitors who  enter your booth the first time  if they were to leave and come back  another time they would need to click on  the booth grading to view it again  the greeting can include an image or  logo and audio  or a welcome video the specifications  are listed below  each option section 14 is logos and  custom colors  we'll need your website logo and booth  logo the booth logo is the most  important  and the specs for each are listed you  can also choose the primary and  secondary colors that we can inject  within your booth  we'll just need the hex or rgb code for  your primary and secondary colors  to adjust within the booth template that  you chose  section 15 is the broadcast messages  this option lets you schedule one  announcement event wide  per day and can be linked to your booth  please contact your sales representative  if you want to schedule more pages 7 and  8 are your booth assets  section 16 are the web links to any  external or company urls  that you would like to provide in your  booth for attendees to visit  we'll just need the web link title a  description and url  if you have more urls that can be listed  in the booth grid  you can create a separate file such as a  word document or an excel spreadsheet of  the additional  web links for your booth section 17 is  literature all pdf documents are listed  here with the category  the title description and file name to  match it with the appropriate literature  title  section 18 is the presentation or  webinars  this is the area where you can provide a  link to your presentations or webinars  or your video files we'll just need your  presentation title  description and either url to webcast  such as  youtube or vimeo or the actual file name  for your.mov.mp4.mpegor.wmv files  this last section is a survey that your  attendees can take within your booth  option 1 allows you to provide the url  to an existing survey  you have already built option 2 allows  us to build a survey for  you through surveymonkey with the survey  title questions and  answers you provide  on behalf of lab roots we are excited to  be working with you in putting together  your company's  virtual booth for the upcoming virtual  event  thank you
 

